# Construction module map

**Acceptance SSOT:** [Construction-Acceptance-System](../../../docs/acceptance/Construction-Acceptance-System.md) · [Product-Readiness](../../../docs/acceptance/Construction-Product-Readiness-Matrix.md) · edition [`docs/editions/construction.yaml`](../../../docs/editions/construction.yaml)

| Domain | API prefix | Notes |
|--------|------------|-------|
| Auth / SSO | `app/api/auth/` | local + SSO |
| Projects | `app/api/projects/` | gantt, daily logs, punch list, plan-vs-actual |
| Progress acts | `progress-acts/` | approve workflow |
| Materials | `material-requisitions/` | site requisitions |
| CDE | `app/api/cde/documents` | common data environment |
| Equipment | `equipment/hours` | machine hours |
| Timesheets | `timesheets/import` | labor import |
| Subcontractors | `subcontractor-claims` | claims per project |
| Events | `events/dispatch` | orchestrator |
| Internal | `GET/POST /api/internal/v1/organization/bind`, `GET/POST /api/internal/v1/runtime-config` | Orch Sync bind + desired-state config; `instrumentation` boot |

**Tenancy (CP-TENANT-01):** `organizationId` on tenant/ops models + kit Prisma extension + `requireSatelliteModule("industry_construction")` (AC-CON-TENANT 🟡 — not live SHARED pool).

| Access matrix (CN-RBAC-01) | `app/api/admin/roles`, `admin/roles/[code]`, `admin/roles/[code]/permissions`, `api/internal/v1/workforce/roles`, `admin/users`, `auth/me`, `auth/session/refresh-permissions`, `auth/logout`; page `/admin/access` | `Role` (`isSystem`, `cloneFromCode`, `permissionCatalogVersion`), `SatelliteAuditLog`; catalog `src/lib/auth/permissions.ts`; page map `page-route-permissions.ts`; API map `api-route-permissions.ts` |

**RBAC Variant A (CN-RBAC-01):** `getSatelliteSession()` also builds `permissions` from the role row and checks the stamped API path against `api-route-permissions.ts` (unlisted → 403). Pages: middleware `authorizePage` + `page-route-permissions.ts`. A new staff route or page needs a catalog row in the same change. Progress act approve is `api:acts.approve`; the APPROVED reopen refusal stays a domain rule. ADR construction-domain-permissions-and-rbac.
